A game's window refits the screen when the Mac's display mode changes while it plays.

This repository's patch to win32u and winemac (version 1), to be offered to WineHQ. It is mavrik's own; nothing is
copied. It uses upstream Wine's own machinery for emulated display modes (win32u's virtual and raw monitor rects,
map_window_rects_virt_to_raw and update_window_state, Wine 9 and later) and changes only when it runs. Upstream
Wine master (checked 2026-11-03: dlls/win32u/defwnd.c, dlls/winemac.drv/display.c and gdi.c, and Proton's
bleeding-edge and proton_10.0 defwnd.c) has the same code, so the fault is upstream's too, on X11 as on the Mac.

The fault: with EmulateModeset=y, which mavrik sets in every prefix, a mode change made outside Wine (System
Settings' "Larger Text", another app, a display that changes its mode) keeps the game's virtual mode and changes
only the physical one (win32u add_modes). The desktop window's WM_DISPLAYCHANGE handler compared only the virtual
screen rect, found it unchanged and returned, so update_children_window_state never ran and every window kept its
old raw rect. In mavrik's S222 lab, switching a 14-inch MacBook Pro from 1512x982 to 1352x878 points for 20 s left
ABZU (DXMT) and Civ VI (D3DMetal) full screen at 0,0 1512x982 and Rogue Legacy (OpenGL) windowed at 76,75 1360x800,
so the picture was cut off at the right and bottom until the mode came back.

Now:
- win32u: the desktop also compares the raw virtual screen rect and, when only that changed, updates its children's
  window state (no SetWindowPos on itself, since its virtual rect is the same). Each window is mapped onto the new
  raw screen the way upstream maps a game's own emulated mode: a full-screen window covers the new screen, and the
  rest of the desktop scales with it, centred, as a graphics card's scaler shows a mode on a panel of another size.
  The game sees no change: its mode, its window rect and its client size stay the same, no WM_DISPLAYCHANGE or
  WM_SIZE reaches it, so it resets nothing; its swapchain draws as before and the presenter scales into the view.
- winemac: each GUI thread that gets a DISPLAYS_CHANGED event resets the process's cached desktop rect and checks
  the Retina state again, as macdrv_ChangeDisplaySettings already does after its own change, so with RetinaMode=y
  the monitors the desktop reads and the frames the game's process sets agree on the new mode (Retina mode is on
  only in the mode Wine started in; Wine bug 42973). The cache is marked valid again once recomputed, so it is not
  recomputed on every window move afterwards.
On Windows the system sends WM_DISPLAYCHANGE to every top-level window and the program decides; under an emulated
mode the program's display did not change, so the scaler's behaviour is the faithful one.

Checked (mavrik S222 lab): applies after patches 0001 to 0043 with no fuzz; win32u.so and winemac.so build with the
engine's toolchain and configure with no new warning, and without this patch both rebuild byte-identical to
revision 12's. The live resolution rows are run by the main session (lab-s222/res-patch/design.md).

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
index 4d55ed53..67c7d92f 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
@@ -3039,15 +3039,20 @@ LRESULT desktop_window_proc( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam, LPARAM lparam,
         return 0;
     case WM_DISPLAYCHANGE:
     {
-        static RECT virtual_rect = {INT_MIN,INT_MIN,INT_MAX,INT_MAX};
+        static RECT virtual_rect = {INT_MIN,INT_MIN,INT_MAX,INT_MAX}, raw_rect = {INT_MIN,INT_MIN,INT_MAX,INT_MAX};
 
         RECT new_rect = get_virtual_screen_rect( 0, MDT_DEFAULT ), old_rect = virtual_rect;
+        RECT new_raw_rect = get_virtual_screen_rect( 0, MDT_RAW_DPI );
         UINT context, flags = 0;
 
-        if (EqualRect( &new_rect, &old_rect )) return TRUE;
+        /* With emulated display modes, a host mode change keeps the virtual screen and changes
+         * only the raw one: the windows still need mapping onto the new raw screen. */
+        if (EqualRect( &new_rect, &old_rect ) && EqualRect( &new_raw_rect, &raw_rect )) return TRUE;
         virtual_rect = new_rect;
+        raw_rect = new_raw_rect;
 
-        TRACE( "desktop %p change from %s to %s\n", hwnd, wine_dbgstr_rect( &old_rect ), wine_dbgstr_rect( &new_rect ) );
+        TRACE( "desktop %p change from %s to %s, raw %s\n", hwnd, wine_dbgstr_rect( &old_rect ),
+               wine_dbgstr_rect( &new_rect ), wine_dbgstr_rect( &new_raw_rect ) );
 
         if (new_rect.right - new_rect.left == old_rect.right - old_rect.left &&
             new_rect.bottom - new_rect.top == old_rect.bottom - old_rect.top)
@@ -3055,11 +3060,14 @@ LRESULT desktop_window_proc( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam, LPARAM lparam,
         if (new_rect.left == old_rect.left && new_rect.top == old_rect.top)
             flags |= SWP_NOMOVE;
 
-        context = NtUserSetThreadDpiAwarenessContext( NTUSER_DPI_PER_MONITOR_AWARE );
-        NtUserSetWindowPos( hwnd, 0, new_rect.left, new_rect.top,
-                            new_rect.right - new_rect.left, new_rect.bottom - new_rect.top,
-                            flags | SWP_NOZORDER | SWP_NOACTIVATE | SWP_DEFERERASE );
-        NtUserSetThreadDpiAwarenessContext( context );
+        if (flags != (SWP_NOSIZE | SWP_NOMOVE))
+        {
+            context = NtUserSetThreadDpiAwarenessContext( NTUSER_DPI_PER_MONITOR_AWARE );
+            NtUserSetWindowPos( hwnd, 0, new_rect.left, new_rect.top,
+                                new_rect.right - new_rect.left, new_rect.bottom - new_rect.top,
+                                flags | SWP_NOZORDER | SWP_NOACTIVATE | SWP_DEFERERASE );
+            NtUserSetThreadDpiAwarenessContext( context );
+        }
 
         update_children_window_state( hwnd );
 
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/display.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/display.c
index ba95f6ec..41566829 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/display.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/display.c
@@ -1087,6 +1087,12 @@ void macdrv_displays_changed(const macdrv_event *event)
 {
     HWND hwnd = NtUserGetDesktopWindow();
 
+    /* A change made outside Wine (System Settings, another app) leaves this process's
+       desktop rect and Retina state stale, so refresh them as ChangeDisplaySettings does
+       after its own change, before the monitors are read again (Wine bug 42973). */
+    macdrv_reset_device_metrics();
+    macdrv_get_desktop_rect();
+
     /* A system display change will get delivered to all GUI-attached threads,
        so the desktop-window-owning thread will get it and all others should
        ignore it.  A synthesized display change event due to activation
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
index 9cf415b5..999551ec 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
@@ -98,6 +98,7 @@ CGRect macdrv_get_desktop_rect(void)
     {
         check_retina_status();
         compute_desktop_rect();
+        device_data_valid = true;
     }
     ret = desktop_rect;
 
